<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">trap</ansi>

Some locked exits and containers are trapped. Finding and clearing them
is a rogue's (and other trap-trained companions') trade.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">trap sense [exit or container]</ansi>
  Search the room, or one exit or container, for traps. Whoever in your
  company is best at it tries. There's a short wait before you can search
  again.

  <ansi fg="command">trap disarm [exit or container]</ansi>
  Try to clear a trap you've found. Success keeps it clear for about a
  day; fail badly and it springs on whoever tried it, so don't try a trap far
  beyond your company's skill.

Your company also senses traps for you automatically as you walk into a
room, and gets one free look the moment you start picking a trapped lock
- turn either off with <ansi fg="command">autoskill</ansi> (<ansi fg="command">help
autoskill</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help autoskill</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help picklock</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help lock</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>.